-- title:
--   Depth dual of a principal divisor lies in the Gram image
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, so that its residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` has characteristic $q$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\kappa$-modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q N κ`; let `data` consist of a monic bivariate modular polynomial $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the pair $(j, j_q)$, with `hKr` the congruence $\Phi \bmod q = (C X^q - X)(C X - X^q)$; let `hα`, `hβ` assert integrality of the two degeneracy embeddings from level $N$ to level $Nq$; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` of places and degree-zero Picard groups from level $N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` along the residue map of $A$, and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple` for $P$ satisfying `IsModel` (the two divisor laws and the cusp laws at $\infty$ and $0$), `OrderLawFixed`, and the regularity and node-value laws for $W$. Assume given, for each $w \in W$: a number field $K_w \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$, node coordinates $(x_w, y_w)$ over $K_w$ at $w$ (each lying in the node integers localised in the field generated by $K_w$, with $x_w$ reducing to $0$ on the first branch and of order $1$ on the Frobenius-translated second branch, and $y_w$ symmetrically), an element $\varpi_w$ of $A \cap K_w$ generating the kernel of the reduction `redRestrict` on $A \cap K_w$, the value-integrality law at $w$ (values at places above $w$ of node integers lie in $A$), and an exponent $E \ge 1$ and a unit $u$ with $x_w y_w = \varpi_w^E u$ in the node integers over $K_w$. Let $e' > 0$, let $D$ be a divisor of the level-$Nq$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is principal, each place $V$ of whose support is strict of the first kind, strict of the second kind, or satisfies $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V \in W$, and let $\mathrm{depth}$ be a natural-number weight on places with $v_A(y_w(V))^{e'} = v_A(q)^{\mathrm{depth}(V)}$ whenever $V$ is in the support of $D$ and reduces to $w \in W$ on the first branch. Then for every pair $s_0$ in `nodePairsOfPlaces (arithFrobC q κ N) W` (the image of $W$ under $w \mapsto (w, \mathrm{Frob}\cdot w)$), the functional
--   $$\textstyle\sum_{s} \bigl(\sum_V D(V)\,\mathrm{depth}(V)\bigr)_{s_1}\,\chi_s \; + \; \deg(D^{\mathrm{II}})\cdot \bigl(e'\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}(q,N,s_{0,1})\bigr)\,\chi_{s_0},$$
--   where $D^{\mathrm{II}}$ is the part of $D$ supported at places strict of the second kind and $\chi_s$ is the coordinate functional at $s$, lies in the image of the Gram map of the pairing $\langle D, D'\rangle = \sum_s e'\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}(q,N,s_1)\,D(s)D'(s)$ on the character lattice of the set of node pairs.
--
--   This is the depth law for principal divisors at an arbitrary prime $q$, with node widths given by the characteristic-$q$ quantity `placeWidthChar`: it identifies the depth functional of a principal divisor, corrected at one node pair by the degree of its second-kind part, as a value of the monodromy (Gram) pairing on the character lattice of the supersingular node pairs. It feeds the computation of the image of a Hecke-generated divisor class in the component group of the Jacobian at $q$, being cited by the two `componentGroupProj` statements for good and for small-prime divisors.
